2026-09-27T12:05:48.2336687Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2337210Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2338480Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2339958Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2340120Z Update Note
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2340445Z ===========
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2340918Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2341393Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2341557Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2341907Z ================
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2342122Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2342394Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2343043Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2343429Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2343609Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2344091Z ====================================
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2344407Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2344654Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2345321Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2346238Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2347367Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2348267Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2348450Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2349117Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2350064Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2350539Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2351044Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2351713Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2351860Z Packages
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2352174Z ========
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2430170Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2432517Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2434984Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2435394Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2436563Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2437867Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2438959Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2439922Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2440678Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2441401Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2441580Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2442001Z ==========================
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2442248Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2444135Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2464348Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2465067Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2466370Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T12:05:48.2466736Z 
